-- title:
--   Kernel ideals and endomorphism rings via finite idèles
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of prime characteristic $q'$ which is algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, and let $X_0$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ such that multiplication by $q'$ is injective on the affine points of $X_0$ over $\kappa$. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'`, that is $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division ring precisely when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $\Lambda\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order (it contains $1$, is multiplicatively closed, is finitely generated, spans the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, and is maximal among such submodules under inclusion), and let $\theta$ be an injective ring homomorphism from `rationalEndSubring κ X₀` — the subring of additive endomorphisms of the points of $X_0$ over $\kappa$ generated by the rationally represented ones — onto $\Lambda$ as its range. Let $W$ be a further elliptic curve over $\kappa$ and $\chi$ a nonzero additive map from the points of $X_0$ to those of $W$ lying in `rationalHomSet κ X₀ W` (zero or rationally represented). Then there exist a unit $d$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ and a unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{f}}$ (the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$) such that the $\theta$-image of the kernel ideal set of $\chi$ — the set of elements of `rationalEndSubring κ X₀` of the form $\rho\circ\chi$ with $\rho\in$ `rationalHomSet κ W X₀` — equals the image under quaternion conjugation `star` of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap x\widehat{\Lambda})$, where $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap x\widehat{\Lambda}$ is [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele Λ x`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19), the preimage in the algebra of the left translate by $x$ of the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes \alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ an everywhere-integral finite adele; and moreover there is an injective ring homomorphism $\theta_W$ from `rationalEndSubring κ W` into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ whose range is exactly $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap x\widehat{\Lambda}x^{-1}$, that is [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele Λ x`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31).
--
--   This is the adelic form of Deuring's and Waterhouse's description of isogenies of supersingular elliptic curves by kernel ideals: every nonzero rationally represented map out of $X_0$ has kernel ideal a conjugate-translated locally principal right ideal $\mathbb{H}\cap x\widehat{\Lambda}$, and the endomorphism ring of the target is the corresponding conjugated order $\mathbb{H}\cap x\widehat{\Lambda}x^{-1}$. It feeds the Čerednik–Drinfel'd package, where the supersingular points of a curve in characteristic $q'$ are matched with a double-coset class set of the definite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q'$.
